## Why This Is Asked
This question validates the ability to design an automated security response system for multi-tenant Azure SaaS environments, integrating threat detection with immediate containment and recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Anomaly detection using Defender for Cloud analytics and Sentinel ML models
- Event Grid-based alert routing and per-tenant processing
- Automated resource isolation via NSG rules, private endpoint restrictions, and conditional access policies
- Key Vault credential rotation and token revocation workflows
- Deployment slot rollback with feature flag coordination
- Comprehensive audit trails across all security actions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-logic for automated breach response
async function handleSecurityAlert(alert) {
  if (alert.severity > 3) {
    await isolateTenantResources(alert.tenantId);
    await rotateCompromisedCredentials(alert.tenantId);
    await initiateSafeRollback(alert.tenantId);
  }
}
```

This question evaluates practical incident response design at scale using Azure native tools, with emphasis on detection integration across multiple services, data immutability for forensic integrity, automated containment mechanisms, and safe rollback strategies. It tests real-world decision-making in complex multi-service environments.

Key Concepts:
- Incident response lifecycle, telemetry aggregation, and automated playbooks
- Data immutability, audit trails, and legal hold requirements
- Network and runtime containment strategies for AKS and App Service
- Canary deployments, feature flags, and rollback safety mechanisms
- Runbook development and post-incident learning processes

Code Example:
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for automated containment trigger
const threatDetected = await Sentinel.evaluateThreat(signal);
if (threatDetected.severity >= 'high') {
  await LogicApp.triggerContainment({
